## Why This Is Asked
The prompt tests ability to design a robust, offline-first telemetry system with crash safety, reliable uploads, and pragmatic data modeling.

## Key Concepts
- Offline persistence with Core Data or SQLite for log durability
- Session-scoped aggregation and de-dup payload hashing
- Resilient queue with exponential backoff and idempotent uploads
- Background URLSession transfers and crash-resilience
- Combine-based publishers for live UI updates

## Code Example
```swift
import Foundation
import CoreData

class LogRecord: NSManagedObject {
  @NSManaged var id: UUID
  @NSManaged var sessionId: UUID
  @NSManaged var timestamp: Date
  @NSManaged var level: String
  @NSManaged var message: String
  @NSManaged var payloadHash: String
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test crash-resilience and data integrity across app relaunches?
- How would you handle user privacy when logs contain PII and ensure compliance with app privacy policies?
